<p>President Donald Trump attended a “dignified transfer” at Dover Air Force Base in Delaware for the remains of six U.S. service members killed in a drone/unmanned aircraft system attack in Kuwait, as their flag-draped cases were carried from a military transport aircraft. The ceremony brought the families of the fallen together with military personnel and senior U.S. leaders in a solemn moment of national mourning and respect. Multiple outlets said the troops died March 1 in an unmanned aircraft system/drone strike in Kuwait, and several sources blamed Iran as the conflict/war with Iran escalated. At Dover, Trump saluted during the transfer and called the service members “great heroes”.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/P_a62vCCJMPOMGEr4SpsYJn_lnD3TZF4ejc5pnxtNwvgu-BX9SeOS2srSG1Ie50xP4fAaO_g66PIcJ_S24csVNdfDk4yS5pHUBkQQGf-UT24ndUZINGQmJCrL_DF3Pe6YaBOl3zw83b2KkSnDed1BKwzWjTIZEyEx4dR0jNV6XOT2npyKQY3x7l_2Ca2_M16ZK_HhvHUKW0F9AoXeUsaDuSNvbVV_XKbOBso' alt='President Donald Trump salutes as service members carry flag-draped cases during a dignified transfer at Dover Air Force Base.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Service branch: Al Jazeera described the fallen troops as U.S. Army soldiers killed in an Iranian drone strike.</li><li>First fatalities: Al-Monitor and Firstpost described them as the first U.S. troops killed in the escalating war with Iran.</li><li>Ceremony details: Several outlets said Trump wore a white “USA” cap during the Dover ceremony.</li><li>Strategy: CBS and Al-Monitor said Trump would not change U.S. strategy in the conflict.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/07/trump-us-service-members-killed-kuwait'>Trump joins families of six slain US service members at Dover air force base</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/dignified-transfer-soldiers-killed-iran-trump-dover/'>Trump salutes as 6 soldiers killed in Iran are transferred back to the U.S.</a> - cbsnews.com<